    <h2 class="section-title h5 mt-4" data-i18n="privacy.hosting.title">Hosting</h2>
    <p class="text-muted" data-i18n="[html]privacy.hosting.desc">
      This website is a static site hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street,
      San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you open a page, your browser connects to GitHub's servers, which receive your
      IP address and technical request data (such as browser type, requested page, and time) in order to deliver the
      website. According to GitHub, the IP addresses of visitors to GitHub Pages sites are logged and stored for security
      purposes. This may involve a transfer of personal data to the USA. GitHub is certified under the EU-U.S. Data
      Privacy Framework, for which the European Commission has adopted an adequacy decision (Art. 45 GDPR). All fonts,
      scripts, and images of this website are delivered via GitHub Pages; apart from the services described below, the
      website does not load any content from third parties. Further information can be found in the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title h5 mt-4" data-i18n="privacy.visit.title">Access statistics</h2>
    <p class="text-muted" data-i18n="privacy.visit.desc">
      When visiting this website, the following data is automatically collected and stored on TU Chemnitz servers for a maximum of 30 days:
    </p>
    <ul class="text-muted">
      <li data-i18n="privacy.visit.ip">IP address</li>
      <li data-i18n="privacy.visit.ua">User-Agent string (identifies browser and possibly operating system)</li>
      <li data-i18n="privacy.visit.referrer">Referrer URL (the web address that refers to our site)</li>
      <li data-i18n="privacy.visit.datetime">Date and time</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-muted" data-i18n="privacy.visit.purpose">
      These data have a personal reference due to the combination of time and IP address, but are necessary to identify
      potential disruptors and thus ensure trouble-free operation. After anonymization by omitting the IP address, we
      gain insights into the use of the website, e.g., how many users visit the website, which pages are popular, and
      from which websites visitors come here. This information primarily serves the technical and editorial further
      development.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title h5 mt-4" data-i18n="privacy.services.title">BirdNET data services</h2>
    <p class="text-muted" data-i18n="privacy.services.desc">
      Some pages load content directly from BirdNET servers operated by TU Chemnitz (birdnet.cornell.edu and birdnet.tu-chemnitz.de): current
      observation statistics on the BirdNET App page, and species images on the BirdNET App page, in the browser demo,
      and in the projects map. Your browser transmits your IP address and technical request data to these servers. This
      data is used only to deliver the requested content. Audio that you analyze in the browser demo is processed
      entirely in your browser and is not uploaded.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title h5 mt-4" data-i18n="privacy.legalBasis.title">Legal basis</h2>
    <p class="text-muted" data-i18n="privacy.legalBasis.desc">
      The legal basis for the processing described in the sections Hosting, Access statistics, and BirdNET data services
      is Art. 6(1)(e) and (3) GDPR in conjunction with Section 3 of the Saxon Data Protection Implementation Act
      (SächsDSDG): providing this website and its services and ensuring their secure operation is part of the public
      tasks of TU Chemnitz in research, teaching, and knowledge transfer.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title h5 mt-4" data-i18n="privacy.map.title">Projects map (OpenStreetMap)</h2>
    <p class="text-muted" data-i18n="[html]privacy.map.desc">
      Our projects map displays map tiles from OpenStreetMap, provided by the OpenStreetMap Foundation (OSMF), United
      Kingdom, via a global network of cache servers. The map is only loaded after you click “Accept and Load Map”. Your
      browser then requests the map tiles directly from OpenStreetMap’s servers and transmits your IP address, browser
      information (user agent), and the address of the page you are viewing (referrer) to the OSMF. The legal basis is
      your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). Your choice is saved in your browser’s local storage so that the map loads
      automatically on later visits; you can withdraw your consent at any time by deleting the stored site data in your
      browser. Further information can be found in the
      <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OSMF privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title h5 mt-4" data-i18n="privacy.storage.title">Data stored in your browser</h2>
    <p class="text-muted" data-i18n="privacy.storage.desc">
      This website does not use cookies or tracking technologies. It stores information in your browser's local storage
      only in two cases: your chosen language, if you select a language or open a link with a language setting, and your
      consent to load the projects map. This information remains on your device and can be deleted at any time in your
      browser settings. The legal basis is Section 25(2) No. 2 TDDDG, as this storage is strictly necessary to provide the
      function you requested.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title h5 mt-4" data-i18n="privacy.links.title">Links to other websites</h2>
    <p class="text-muted" data-i18n="privacy.links.desc">
      Links to other websites (for example GitHub, YouTube, or app stores) open in a new tab. No data is transmitted to
      these providers until you click such a link; after that, the privacy policy of the respective provider applies.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title h5 mt-4" data-i18n="privacy.rights.title">Your rights</h2>
    <p class="text-muted" data-i18n="privacy.rights.desc">
      You have the right to access the personal data concerning you (Art. 15 GDPR), to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR), to
      erasure (Art. 17 GDPR), to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR), and to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR). You
      also have the right to object at any time, on grounds relating to your particular situation, to processing based on
      Art. 6(1)(e) GDPR (Art. 21 GDPR). Where processing is based on your consent, you can withdraw it at any time with
      effect for the future (Art. 7(3) GDPR). To exercise your rights, please contact the controller or the data
      protection officer named above.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title h5 mt-4" data-i18n="privacy.complaint.title">Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
